=product @PRODUCER@ @BASE@ @PRODUCT@ @PCSIVERSION@ full
1 'PRODUCER
=prompt @PRODUCER@
1 'PRODUCT
=prompt SQLite @VERSION@ for OpenVMS (vms-sqlite)
1 'NOTICE
=prompt SQLite and this port are in the public domain.
1 RELEASE_NOTES
=prompt Documentation is in [VMSSQLITE.DOC]README.VMS under the installation directory.
1 POST_INSTALL
=prompt Post-installation tasks for SQLite for OpenVMS (vms-sqlite)
    VMSSQLITE$ROOT and SQLITE3$SHR are defined now (system logical names).
    At boot, add to SYS$MANAGER:SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM:
    $ @SYS$STARTUP:VMSSQLITE$STARTUP.COM
    The DCL symbol sqlite3, from LOGIN.COM or SYLOGIN.COM:
    $ @VMSSQLITE$ROOT:[COM]VMSSQLITE$SETUP
    Building against SQLite: compile with /INCLUDE=VMSSQLITE$ROOT:[INCLUDE]
    and link with VMSSQLITE$ROOT:[LIB]LIBSQLITE3.OLB/LIBRARY, or with
    SQLITE3$SHR/SHAREABLE in an options file (README.VMS).

PRODUCT REMOVE VMSSQLITE deassigns VMSSQLITE$ROOT and SQLITE3$SHR.
